# Files that are gitignored but still have to be in a new worktree.
#
# Claude Code puts every parallel session in its own git worktree (the Code tab
# of the desktop app does it for every new session). A worktree is a fresh
# checkout, so gitignored files are not in it — and without .env the app does
# not start there. Everything listed here is copied along.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore syntax. Only files that match AND are gitignored are
# copied, so nothing that is in the repo anyway gets duplicated.

.env
.env.local

# Deliberately NOT in here: .dev/ — that is the running app's scratch state
# (its port, its log). A second session needs its own, not a copy of the first
# one's. The database is not a file either; it runs in Docker and all sessions
# share it (docker-compose.yml).
